<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτᾱνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>winged, flying,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ποτανοῖς</span> among <i>fowls,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				3.80
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. οἰωνοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1478
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέδιλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					460
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. εἴ σέ τις θεῶν κτίσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					620
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				1142
			</span></i> (lyr.): prov. of vain pursuits, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διώκει παῖς ποτανὸν ὄρνιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					394
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτανὸς ἐν
				Μοίσαισι,</span> i.e. <i>soaring</i> in the arts of the
			Muses, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				5.114
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτανᾷ μαχανᾷ</span> by
				<i>soaring</i> art, i.e. by poesy, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>N.</u>
				7.22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμᾷ ποτανὸς ἀμφὶ μαχανᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>P.</u>
					8.34
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταναὶ</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτ᾽ αἰναὶ</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> τευθίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					61
				</span></i>
			.—
				Dor.
			 for <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτηνός</span></b> ,
			which occurs only in Poet. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				252b
			</span></i>.</div>
